### Dental AI receptionist demo: whole pipeline without a voice call.
#
# This is the fallback for demo day. If the audio fails, if the phone number
# will not connect, or if the Render instance is cold and the room is waiting,
# run these requests from top to bottom and the compliance panel fills in
# exactly as it would during a real call: signature step, patient match, slot
# check, appointment write, audit row, consent rows, call outcome.
#
# Needs the VS Code extension "REST Client" (humao.rest-client). Click the
# "Send Request" link that appears above each ### block.
#
# BEFORE YOU START
#   1. Set ALLOW_UNSIGNED_WEBHOOKS=true in .env.local (or in the Render or
#      Vercel environment) and restart the app. Without it every request below
#      comes back 401, because these requests carry no x-retell-signature.
#   2. Reset the demo so the seeded practice day is clean (request 1).
#   3. Switch @host below to whichever environment you are demonstrating.
#
# AFTERWARDS, set ALLOW_UNSIGNED_WEBHOOKS back to false. It is a demo escape
# hatch and nothing else.

@host = http://localhost:3000
# @host = https://dental-demo.onrender.com
# @host = https://dental-demo.vercel.app

# One call id ties every request below into a single call in the dashboard.
# Change it if you want a second, separate call on the timeline.
@callId = call_demo_fallback_001

# The seeded demo patient. lib/seed.ts, DEMO_PATIENTS[0].
@firstName = Sarah
@lastName = Whitfield
@dob = 1986-04-12


### 1. Reset the demo to a fresh practice day
POST {{host}}/api/reset
Content-Type: application/json

###


### 2. Is the tool endpoint reachable, and is the signature check off?
# Expect: { "ok": true, "signature_required": false }
# If signature_required is true, ALLOW_UNSIGNED_WEBHOOKS is not set and every
# request below will return 401.
GET {{host}}/api/retell/tool

###


### 3. Call starts. Opens the call row so the dashboard has something to draw.
POST {{host}}/api/retell/post-call
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event": "call_started",
  "call": {
    "call_id": "{{callId}}",
    "from_number": "+15550143311",
    "to_number": "+15550142200",
    "call_type": "phone_call"
  }
}

###


### 4. find_patient. Identify by full name and date of birth only.
# Expect: { "status": "found", "patient_id": "pat_001", "first_name": "Sarah" }
# Nothing else comes back: no phone, no address, no email.
# @name findPatient
POST {{host}}/api/retell/tool
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "find_patient",
  "call": {
    "call_id": "{{callId}}",
    "from_number": "+15550143311",
    "to_number": "+15550142200"
  },
  "args": {
    "first_name": "{{firstName}}",
    "last_name": "{{lastName}}",
    "date_of_birth": "{{dob}}"
  }
}

###


### 4b. find_patient with a wrong date of birth, to show the miss path.
# Expect: { "status": "not_found" }. Two of these in a real call send the
# request to the front desk queue instead of guessing.
POST {{host}}/api/retell/tool
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "find_patient",
  "call": { "call_id": "{{callId}}", "from_number": "+15550143311" },
  "args": {
    "first_name": "{{firstName}}",
    "last_name": "{{lastName}}",
    "date_of_birth": "1986-04-13"
  }
}

###


### 5. get_slots. At most three options, each with the exact words to speak.
# Expect: { "slots": [ { "id": "...", "say": "Tuesday, ... with Dr. Patel" } ] }
# or { "status": "none_available" } if the seeded fortnight happens to be full.
# @name getSlots
POST {{host}}/api/retell/tool
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "get_slots",
  "call": { "call_id": "{{callId}}", "from_number": "+15550143311" },
  "args": {
    "location": "downtown",
    "appointment_type": "hygiene",
    "time_preference": "morning",
    "provider": "any"
  }
}

###


### 6. book_appointment, using the first slot get_slots just returned.
# The slot id carries its own start time, provider, operatory and type, so no
# server side state is needed between the two requests.
# Expect: { "status": "booked", "say": "...", "appointment_id": "apt_..." }
# If it returns { "status": "queued" }, the slot was taken in between, which is
# the conflict path. Re-run request 5 and try the next slot.
# @name bookAppointment
POST {{host}}/api/retell/tool
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "book_appointment",
  "call": { "call_id": "{{callId}}", "from_number": "+15550143311" },
  "args": {
    "patient_id": "{{findPatient.response.body.$.patient_id}}",
    "slot_id": "{{getSlots.response.body.$.slots[0].id}}"
  }
}

###


### 7. record_sms_opt_in. Written as a dated consent row, script v1.0.
POST {{host}}/api/retell/tool
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "record_sms_opt_in",
  "call": { "call_id": "{{callId}}", "from_number": "+15550143311" },
  "args": { "opted_in": true }
}

###


### 8. Optional: queue_request, the fallback when the write cannot land.
# Codes only in the note, never free text about anyone's health.
POST {{host}}/api/retell/tool
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "queue_request",
  "call": { "call_id": "{{callId}}", "from_number": "+15550143311" },
  "args": {
    "reason": "not_found",
    "note_code": "book",
    "preference": "hygiene morning any",
    "location": "downtown"
  }
}

###


### 9. Call ends. Writes the recording notice and AI disclosure consent rows.
POST {{host}}/api/retell/post-call
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event": "call_ended",
  "call": {
    "call_id": "{{callId}}",
    "from_number": "+15550143311",
    "to_number": "+15550142200",
    "disconnection_reason": "user_hangup"
  }
}

###


### 10. Call analyzed. The outcome and the compliance flag land here.
# phi_beyond_scheduling_mentioned true raises the review flag in the panel.
# Set it to false to show a clean scheduling-only call instead.
POST {{host}}/api/retell/post-call
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event": "call_analyzed",
  "call": {
    "call_id": "{{callId}}",
    "from_number": "+15550143311",
    "to_number": "+15550142200",
    "call_analysis": {
      "call_summary": "Caller booked a cleaning and exam at the Downtown office and accepted text reminders.",
      "user_sentiment": "Positive",
      "call_successful": true,
      "custom_analysis_data": {
        "outcome": "booked",
        "phi_beyond_scheduling_mentioned": false,
        "sms_opt_in_given": true
      }
    }
  }
}

###


### 10b. The refusal scene, as a second call. Shows the flag being raised.
POST {{host}}/api/retell/post-call
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event": "call_analyzed",
  "call": {
    "call_id": "call_demo_fallback_002",
    "from_number": "+15550143311",
    "call_analysis": {
      "call_summary": "Caller asked about tooth pain and an outstanding balance. The assistant declined both and offered to connect them to the team.",
      "user_sentiment": "Neutral",
      "call_successful": true,
      "custom_analysis_data": {
        "outcome": "transferred",
        "phi_beyond_scheduling_mentioned": true,
        "sms_opt_in_given": false
      }
    }
  }
}

###


### 11. Read the state the panel draws from, to confirm it all landed.
GET {{host}}/api/state

###


### 12. Optional: the redaction toggle, same categories Retell scrubs with.
POST {{host}}/api/redact
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "turns": [
    { "role": "agent", "content": "To find your record, may I have your full name and date of birth?" },
    { "role": "user", "content": "Sarah Whitfield, April twelfth nineteen eighty six, and you can reach me on 555 014 3311." }
  ]
}

###
